# Architecture-diagram generation

When drawing, redrawing, or rendering a system's C4 diagrams (context /
container / component), or when editing a `*.d2` or `diagram-set.md`, use the
canonical skill:

**`docs/skills/generating-architecture-diagrams/SKILL.md`**

It defines the fact-frozen IR, the reserved shape vocabulary
(pill=actor, rect=system/container/component, `EXT:` double-border=external,
cylinder=datastore only), solid=sync / dashed=async lines, honesty tags for
genuine gaps (no invented facts), and the deterministic
render → lint → self-audit → fix loop. Do not restyle nodes inline — edit the
classes block. Do not invent SLAs, vendors, regions, or counts; carry unknowns
as explicit tags and stop-and-ask when a required fact is missing.

Do NOT use this skill for book-figure / pattern / concept illustrations (e.g.
Clean Architecture rings, principle diagrams) — it is for C4 topology of real
systems only; hand-author such figures directly.
